Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.35,0:00:03.90,Default,,0,0,0,,The first time I heard my own voice\Non channel nine, it was begging me
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.92,0:00:05.46,Default,,0,0,0,,not to open the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.49,0:00:07.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Not a voice that sounded like mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.71,0:00:11.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Mine. The same breathless catch\NI get when I try not to panic.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.32,0:00:12.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Then somebody knocked.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.31,0:00:13.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Three slow knocks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.78,0:00:17.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I was alone at Blackpine Relay, a\Nlittle communications station above
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.19,0:00:18.73,Default,,0,0,0,,thirty miles of forest.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.75,0:00:20.95,Default,,0,0,0,,My shift had started an hour earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.98,0:00:22.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I had already done the radio check.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.81,0:00:24.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Blackpine Relay.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.14,0:00:25.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Daniel Reed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.31,0:00:26.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Night shift.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.49,0:00:29.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Now the same speaker was\Nsaying my name back to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.33,0:00:32.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Outside, rain crawled down the window.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.94,0:00:35.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Inside, the wall clock\Nsaid twelve thirteen.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.99,0:00:38.64,Default,,0,0,0,,The voice gave a time four minutes later.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.67,0:00:40.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Twelve seventeen.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.23,0:00:43.94,Default,,0,0,0,,And then it said something I could\Nnot understand until much later.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.97,0:00:46.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Whatever happens, don't let her answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.46,0:00:50.76,Default,,0,0,0,,There was a laminated instruction\Ncard beside the radio.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.78,0:00:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,The official side explained\Nhow to log emergency traffic.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.36,0:00:57.39,Default,,0,0,0,,On the back, somebody had written\None sentence in black marker.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.42,0:00:59.56,Default,,0,0,0,,If you hear yourself, do not answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.58,0:01:01.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought it was a joke\Nleft for the new guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.68,0:01:03.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I pressed the microphone anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.34,0:01:04.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.33,0:01:07.06,Default,,0,0,0,,The red light stayed on\Nafter I released the button.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.08,0:01:09.28,Default,,0,0,0,,From the speaker came a soft breath.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.31,0:01:11.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Then my voice said, You\Njust made it easier.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.71,0:01:13.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I pulled the microphone plug.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.60,0:01:15.38,Default,,0,0,0,,The voice continued.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.94,0:01:18.63,Default,,0,0,0,,In four minutes you're going\Nto break the white mug.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.66,0:01:21.46,Default,,0,0,0,,You're going to find a red\Nkey behind the battery.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.48,0:01:23.35,Default,,0,0,0,,And you're going to call your sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.37,0:01:25.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I looked at the mug beside my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.72,0:01:28.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I had not told anyone at work about Lena.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.55,0:01:31.35,Default,,0,0,0,,The telephone on the desk began to ring.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.31,0:01:33.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I let it ring until it stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.99,0:01:35.34,Default,,0,0,0,,The radio clicked.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.36,0:01:36.96,Default,,0,0,0,,You should have picked up, my voice said.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.99,0:01:37.91,Default,,0,0,0,,She thinks you're angry.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.94,0:01:40.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I stood so quickly my\Nchair caught the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.38,0:01:43.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The mug fell. It struck\Nthe floor in three pieces.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.06,0:01:44.67,Default,,0,0,0,,The clock said twelve seventeen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.70,0:01:45.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Four minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.68,0:01:48.24,Default,,0,0,0,,I told myself somebody\Nhad cameras in the room.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.26,0:01:51.16,Default,,0,0,0,,That somebody was watching\Nme and playing a recording.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.18,0:01:54.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I searched above the shelves, under\Nthe desk, inside the dead security
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.94,0:01:56.65,Default,,0,0,0,,monitor. Nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.67,0:01:59.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I saw the battery at\Nthe back of the radio rack.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.32,0:02:02.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Behind it was a red key.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.18,0:02:04.08,Default,,0,0,0,,One tooth was broken off.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.10,0:02:07.00,Default,,0,0,0,,A little paper tag had gone soft with age.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.03,0:02:10.48,Default,,0,0,0,,On it was a drawing of the steel\Ncabinet in the back hallway.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.50,0:02:12.75,Default,,0,0,0,,From outside came another knock.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.78,0:02:14.73,Default,,0,0,0,,This time it was at the window.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.75,0:02:17.53,Default,,0,0,0,,The glass was ten feet above the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.49,0:02:20.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I called Lena on the landline.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.39,0:02:22.68,Default,,0,0,0,,My cell phone had no service up there.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.70,0:02:25.11,Default,,0,0,0,,She answered on the\Nsecond ring, half asleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.14,0:02:27.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I told her I needed her\Nto stay on the phone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.19,0:02:28.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Not to drive up.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.11,0:02:29.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Just talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.14,0:02:32.10,Default,,0,0,0,,While she asked what was wrong,\Nthe radio made a sound like someone
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.13,0:02:33.38,Default,,0,0,0,,clearing their throat.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.40,0:02:35.10,Default,,0,0,0,,A woman's voice came through.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.13,0:02:36.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Lena's voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.43,0:02:39.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Half a second before she spoke into\Nthe telephone, the radio said the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.55,0:02:40.68,Default,,0,0,0,,same words.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.70,0:02:42.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Daniel, are you hurt?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.11,0:02:43.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I hung up.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.15,0:02:45.07,Default,,0,0,0,,The radio went silent.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.57,0:02:48.64,Default,,0,0,0,,For the first time, the thing\Noutside stopped knocking.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.67,0:02:51.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I understood enough to\Nbe afraid of the wires.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.33,0:02:54.28,Default,,0,0,0,,The antenna cable ran\Nthrough the rear wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.31,0:02:58.18,Default,,0,0,0,,The telephone cable disappeared\Ninto the same steel cabinet.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.21,0:03:00.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I followed them with my flashlight.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.53,0:03:04.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Something wet brushed the other side\Nof the wall, keeping pace with me
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.59,0:03:04.84,Default,,0,0,0,,.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.79,0:03:07.68,Default,,0,0,0,,The red key fitted the cabinet.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.71,0:03:11.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Inside were the antenna switch,\Nthe telephone junction, and a small
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.08,0:03:12.56,Default,,0,0,0,,backup power supply.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.58,0:03:14.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Scratched into the metal\Nwas another warning.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.79,0:03:16.49,Default,,0,0,0,,It follows the open line.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.52,0:03:18.47,Default,,0,0,0,,My voice returned from the front room.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.49,0:03:19.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't touch the antenna.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.61,0:03:20.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm trying to help you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.72,0:03:22.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I turned the switch a quarter turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.39,0:03:24.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The voice stretched, thin and distant.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.61,0:03:27.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Outside, something dragged a\Nfingernail down the window.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.42,0:03:28.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I turned the switch back.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.89,0:03:30.29,Default,,0,0,0,,The scratching stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.32,0:03:32.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Then my voice whispered, Look at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.29,0:03:33.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I should not have looked.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.37,0:03:36.35,Default,,0,0,0,,A man stood beyond the glass.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.37,0:03:37.87,Default,,0,0,0,,My jacket. My haircut.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.90,0:03:38.90,Default,,0,0,0,,My face.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.92,0:03:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,But he was smiling with his mouth\Nclosed, and the shape of the smile
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.36,0:03:43.95,Default,,0,0,0,,moved under his skin.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.97,0:03:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,His right hand was\Npressed against the glass.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.70,0:03:49.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a scar across my left palm.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.07,0:03:51.49,Default,,0,0,0,,His scar was on the wrong hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.45,0:03:53.90,Default,,0,0,0,,The station lights went out.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.92,0:03:55.17,Default,,0,0,0,,The radio did not.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.20,0:03:57.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Its green lamp burned\Non the backup battery.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.90,0:04:00.07,Default,,0,0,0,,The man outside tilted his head.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.10,0:04:03.02,Default,,0,0,0,,In the dark, I heard him speak from\Nthe radio, from the telephone, and
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.05,0:04:04.54,Default,,0,0,0,,from the other side of the window.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.56,0:04:05.61,Default,,0,0,0,,All at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.64,0:04:06.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Cut the power, he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.92,0:04:08.40,Default,,0,0,0,,I opened the cabinet again.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.42,0:04:11.19,Default,,0,0,0,,My flashlight found\Ntwo thick black cables.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.21,0:04:12.85,Default,,0,0,0,,One fed the antenna.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.87,0:04:15.04,Default,,0,0,0,,One fed the telephone junction.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.06,0:04:17.35,Default,,0,0,0,,The red key shook between my fingers.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.37,0:04:19.90,Default,,0,0,0,,From the desk, Lena called my name.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.43,0:04:22.54,Default,,0,0,0,,The receiver was still on its cradle.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.57,0:04:24.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, Daniel. Pick up.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.05,0:04:26.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I reached for the antenna connector.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.24,0:04:28.73,Default,,0,0,0,,The handle of the front\Ndoor began to turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.75,0:04:31.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Slowly. I pulled the cable free.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.34,0:04:34.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Every speaker in the station\Nscreamed with my voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.55,0:04:36.14,Default,,0,0,0,,I dropped the flashlight.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.17,0:04:39.13,Default,,0,0,0,,In the blackness, something\Nheavy struck the front door.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.15,0:04:40.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Then there was silence.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.76,0:04:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I waited until I could\Nhear the rain again.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.03,0:04:45.78,Default,,0,0,0,,The radio light was dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.80,0:04:47.29,Default,,0,0,0,,The telephone was silent.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.32,0:04:48.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing stood at the window.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.76,0:04:51.78,Default,,0,0,0,,I left through the back, climbed\Ninto my car, and kept the headlights
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.80,0:04:53.58,Default,,0,0,0,,off until I reached the road.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.60,0:04:56.58,Default,,0,0,0,,When the dashboard radio\Nlit up, I tore its fuse out.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.60,0:04:59.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I drove down the mountain with\Nboth hands locked on the wheel.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.76,0:05:03.06,Default,,0,0,0,,At the first place my phone\Nfound service, I called Lena.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.08,0:05:04.49,Default,,0,0,0,,It rang once.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.52,0:05:06.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I ended the call\Nbefore she could answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.94,0:05:09.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Whatever happens, don't let her answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.01,0:05:12.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I finally understood that sentence.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.43,0:05:15.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I had thought the voice was\Nwarning me about the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.60,0:05:18.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe it was only teaching me what to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.20,0:05:21.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe it had needed a voice, and\Na reason for me to open another
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.68,0:05:25.71,Default,,0,0,0,,line. I drove the rest of the\Nway without touching the phone
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.73,0:05:25.97,Default,,0,0,0,,.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.98,0:05:29.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Lena's porch light was on when I arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.54,0:05:31.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Her front door stood open.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.04,0:05:32.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I stopped at the bottom of the steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.97,0:05:35.87,Default,,0,0,0,,She appeared in the hallway\Nwearing her blue sleep shirt.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.90,0:05:37.58,Default,,0,0,0,,She looked past me, toward the road.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.61,0:05:39.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Then back at my face.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.11,0:05:40.16,Default,,0,0,0,,How did you get outside?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.18,0:05:43.06,Default,,0,0,0,,she asked. I told her\Nnot to say another word.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.08,0:05:45.77,Default,,0,0,0,,From the upstairs bedroom,\Nmy voice called down.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.80,0:05:47.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Lena? Who are you talking to?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.62,0:05:48.94,Default,,0,0,0,,She began to turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.96,0:05:51.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I caught her wrist and\Npulled her onto the porch.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.57,0:05:54.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Behind her, the telephone started ringing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.89,0:05:56.52,Default,,0,0,0,,She looked at the phone in my hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.54,0:05:57.89,Default,,0,0,0,,The screen was black.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.92,0:05:59.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I wasn't calling.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.25,0:06:01.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Upstairs, bare feet crossed the floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.76,0:06:03.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Slow steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.03,0:06:05.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Then a man laughed with my voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.32,0:06:07.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I had disconnected the antenna.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.25,0:06:09.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I had never touched the telephone line.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.66,0:06:13.03,Default,,0,0,0,,At the top of the stairs,\Nsomething knocked three times.
